e of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, when you use the Simple Past tense, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Within a short time, Jessica <span class=\"strong\">amassed</span> a pen collection that filled up her drawers at home.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is another example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">One day when one of her books fell off the shelf, an idea <span class=\"strong\">hit</span> her. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that there are both regular and irregular verbs. Look at the chart for examples of the Simple Past tense verbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Regular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Irregular Verb</div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Past</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decide\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decided\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"begin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"began\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"amass\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"amassed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hit\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Several years ago, Jessica Bloom, editor of the school newspaper, decided to do something useful with the large number of pens that were being thrown out every day. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Instead of discarding her old pens, Jessica began collecting her pens, along with those of other students in her class."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She took her collection to the local plastic factory and asked them to melt down her pens."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Her classmates loved the idea of a creative way to hold their books on a desk or shelf, and started buying the bookends. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">The company <span class=\"strong\">is helping</span> to save the environment.</span></p><p>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">have begun</span> using the plastic from recycled pens in many of their products. </span></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Our environment <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being affected</span> by junked plastic items.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Recently, her idea <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been taken over</span> by a private design company. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Several years ago, Jessica Bloom, editor of the school newspaper, decided to do something useful with the large number of pens that were being thrown out every day. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our environment is being affected by junked plastic items, like pens. Instead of discarding her old pens, Jessica began collecting her pens, along with those of other students in her class."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They have begun using the plastic from recycled pens in many of their products."}, {"type": "example", "content": "For Jessica and her classmates, this idea has become a method to write their way to a better environment. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to melt down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bheat a \u200bmetal or plastic \u200bobject until it \u200bturns to \u200bliquid "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She took her collection to the local plastic factory and asked them to melt down her pens."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about a proposal to help the environment."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bookend "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one of a pair of objects that you put at the end of a row of books to prevent them from falling over"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She started to design plastic bookends of all different sizes and shapes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take over"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gain control of a company or situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, 